# Documented exceptions for the CI image scan (.github/workflows/image_scan.yml).
# Every entry needs a rationale and a `Revisit:` trigger — enforced by
# spec/code_smells/template_invariants_spec.rb.

# json 2.18.0 still ships INSIDE Ruby 4.0.7 as a default gem (re-checked on the
# 4.0.7 bump); Gemfile.lock pins the fixed json (>= 2.19.2) and Bundler activates
# it at runtime, so the vulnerable copy is dormant until a Ruby patch replaces it.
# Revisit: on the next Ruby 4.0.x patch (bump .tool-versions), or 2026-12-01.
CVE-2026-33210

# Go stdlib v1.26.5 baked into thruster's precompiled binary (0.1.23 in the
# lock; 0.1.25, the newest release, verified built on the SAME go1.26.5).
# One batch of stdlib CVEs, all fixed only in Go 1.26.6+: mostly
# resource-exhaustion (encoding/xml recursion 56859, net/url quadratic parse
# 56860, crypto/tls indefinite KeyUpdate 56862, h2c DoS 56853, dnsmessage
# 46600, 33818) plus html/template XSS (56858) and x/net/idna punycode
# handling (39821) — the latter two live in packages a static-asset proxy
# does not exercise for rendering, but reachability is not load-bearing
# here: no thruster release built on Go >= 1.26.6 exists, so there is no
# action available to us regardless. (The 0.1.22-era CVE-2026-39822 entry
# that previously lived here was cleared by the 0.1.23 rebuild on go1.26.5
# — its Revisit trigger — and removed.)
# 0.1.26 (2026-09-03, this bump) clears the golang.org/x/crypto critical
# (CVE-2026-56854) the scan reported on 0.1.25; whether it also moved past
# go1.26.5 cannot be read from the scan, because ignored findings are not
# printed. Revisit: on the next thruster release (> 0.1.26), or 2026-10-15.
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862
